  "publishedAt": "2026-09-05 21:24:18",
  "releaseNotes": "# AID v2.0.0\n\n## 中文发布说明\n\n### 新增功能\n\n- 新增通用 Skill Runtime，支持 Skill 目录、版本化资源、固定子 Skill、调用、动态澄清、事件续传、运行取消、历史与审计。\n- 内置剧本入口、剧本写作和独立审核 Skill，支持新建、续写、改写、规范化、客观修复，以及项目、剧集和历史运行上下文。\n- 新增供应商余额监控、余额快照、分级告警、提醒人管理和邮件余额日报。\n- 新增账号安全中心能力，包括首次设置密码、双验证码换绑、会话管理、登录历史和注销后的再注册限制。\n- 新增 AI 业务编排统一入口，以及文本模型的多模态输入、流式输出和思考能力配置。\n- 新增受管 Nginx 网关配置与独立 SEO 管理中心，支持安全校验、失败恢复、robots、sitemap 和百度链接提交。\n\n### 优化与修复\n\n- 媒体任务增加不可变终态时间和 ETA 聚合基线，修复终态进度被旧事件覆盖的问题。\n- 角色和道具同一形态统一只保留一张主图；角色自动生图复用现有角色设定卡形态。\n- 文本模型能力迁移只作用于可识别的官方基线，不重置用户自定义模型能力。\n- 管理后台补齐旧版图片、视频、音频和文档输入能力的无损迁移，并修复能力编辑后的往返保存契约。\n- 收紧默认安全配置，Druid 控制台及 Web 统计默认关闭。\n- 生成任务新增错误快照，提示词超长、内容审核失败和批量生成失败等具体原因可在任务详情中稳定查看。\n- 管理后台隐藏重复或内部维护的系统配置分类，相关设置继续由对应业务页面统一管理。\n- Web 登录守卫统一使用安全返回路径，修复直接访问受保护页面时的跳转循环；全新安装和静态资源构建结果保持确定性。\n- Web 首页聚焦 AI 漫剧、AI 电影与 AI 漫画创作入口，作品库保留项目、分集和本地导出能力。\n\n### 数据库与兼容性\n\n- 升级时执行 `sql/v2.0.0.sql`；新安装基线已同步到 `sql/aid-init.sql`。\n- 增量 SQL 兼容 MySQL 5.7、支持重复执行，不要求 `CREATE ROUTINE` 权限。\n- 数据库迁移包含 SEO、Nginx 权限、供应商余额、账号安全、媒体 ETA、模型能力、主图约束、Skill Runtime 和任务错误快照等公共结构。\n- 没有可用文本模型时，Skill 数据结构仍可完成升级，相关 Skill 保持停用，待管理员配置模型后再启用。\n- 升级不会删除历史孤立表或用户业务数据，也不会覆盖合法密钥、倍率和用户自定义提示词。\n\n### 升级注意事项\n\n- 这是主版本升级。升级前必须备份数据库、部署配置、证书和用户媒体目录，并优先在测试环境完成验证。\n- 升级账号需要建表、改表、创建索引和更新数据的权限。\n\n# AID v2.0.0\n\n## English Release Notes\n\n### Features\n\n- Added a general-purpose Skill Runtime with versioned resources, fixed sub-Skills, invocation, clarification, resumable events, cancellation, history, and auditing.\n- Added built-in screenplay entry, writing, and independent review Skills with create, continue, rewrite, normalize, objective-fix, project, episode, and historical-run contexts.\n- Added provider balance monitoring, balance snapshots, severity-based alerts, recipient management, and email balance reports.\n- Added account security capabilities for initial password setup, dual-code rebinding, session management, login history, and post-deletion re-registration restrictions.\n- Added a unified AI orchestration entry and structured multimodal, streaming, and reasoning capabilities for text models.\n- Added managed Nginx gateway configuration and a dedicated SEO console with validation, recovery, robots, sitemap, and Baidu URL submission support.\n\n### Improvements and Fixes\n\n- Added immutable terminal timestamps and ETA aggregation baselines for media tasks, preventing stale events from overwriting terminal progress.\n- Enforced a single primary image per character or prop form and reused the existing character-sheet form for automatic character generation.\n- Limited text-model capability migrations to recognized official baselines without resetting user-defined models.\n- Preserved legacy image, video, audio, and document input capabilities when editing and saving model capabilities in the admin console.\n- Hardened defaults by disabling the Druid console and Web statistics unless explicitly enabled.\n- Added durable task-error snapshots so prompt-length, moderation, and batch-generation failures remain visible in task details.\n- Hid duplicate or internally maintained configuration categories from the system settings page while preserving their existing values and dedicated management pages.\n- Consolidated Web authentication redirects around a safe return path, fixed protected-route redirect loops, and made clean installs and static asset output deterministic.\n- Focused the Web home page on AI comic-drama, AI film, and AI comic creation while retaining project, episode, and local export workflows.\n\n### Database and Compatibility\n\n- Upgrades execute `sql/v2.0.0.sql`; fresh installations use the synchronized `sql/aid-init.sql` baseline.\n- The migration is repeatable, compatible with MySQL 5.7, and does not require `CREATE ROUTINE` privileges.\n- The migration covers public SEO, Nginx permissions, provider balances, account security, media ETA, model capabilities, primary-image consistency, Skill Runtime, and task-error snapshots.\n- Skill schema installation succeeds without an active text model. Built-in Skills remain disabled until an administrator configures a valid model.\n- The migration does not delete historical orphan tables or user business data and does not overwrite valid credentials, multipliers, or user-customized prompts.\n\n### Upgrade Notes\n\n- This is a major-version upgrade. Back up the database, deployment configuration, certificates, and user media before upgrading, and validate the upgrade in a staging environment first.\n- The database account requires permissions to create and alter tables, create indexes, and update data.",
